-- title:
--   In large multidegrees, the Hilbert function of an ideal of products of moment-curve linear forms is at most a coefficient of $\prod_k(X_{u_k}+X_{v_k})$
-- statement:
--   **Setting.** Let $K$ be a field, $\iota$ a finite set of blocks and $a=(a_j)_{j\in\iota}\in\mathbb{N}^\iota$. Let $R=K[x_{j,h} : j\in\iota,\ 0\le h\le a_j]$, so that block $j$ carries the $a_j+1$ homogeneous coordinates of $\mathbb{P}^{a_j}$, multigraded by $\mathbb{Z}^\iota$ with $x_{j,h}$ of multidegree $\mathbf e_j$. For $d\in\mathbb{Z}^\iota$ let $R_d$ be the multihomogeneous polynomials of multidegree $d$, and for an ideal $J$ let $h_J(d)=\dim_KR_d/(J\cap R_d)$. For $j\in\iota$ and $s\in K$ let
--   $$\lambda_j(s)=\sum_{h=0}^{a_j}s^h\,x_{j,h}$$
--   be the linear form in block $j$ whose coefficient vector $(1,s,\dots,s^{a_j})$ lies on the moment curve. A *factor pair* is a pair of polynomials $(\ell,r)$ together with multidegrees $\delta,\delta'\in\mathbb{Z}^\iota$ such that $\ell$ is multihomogeneous of multidegree $\delta$ and $r$ of multidegree $\delta'$.
--
--   **Statement.** Let $(\ell_1,r_1),\dots,(\ell_M,r_M)$ be factor pairs with recorded left multidegrees $\delta_1,\dots,\delta_M$, let $u,v:\{1,\dots,M\}\to\iota$, and let $t:\{1,\dots,M\}\times\{0,1\}\to K$ be injective, such that
--   - $\ell_k=\lambda_{u_k}(t_{k,0})$ and $r_k=\lambda_{v_k}(t_{k,1})$ for every $k$;
--   - every entry of every $\delta_k$ is at most $1$;
--   - $M=\sum_{j\in\iota}a_j$.
--
--   Let $J$ be the ideal generated by $\ell_1r_1,\dots,\ell_Mr_M$, and let $d\in\mathbb{Z}^\iota$ satisfy $d_j>M$ for every $j$. Then
--   $$h_J(d)\ \le\ [X^a]\prod_{k=1}^M\bigl(X_{u_k}+X_{v_k}\bigr),$$
--   the coefficient of the monomial $X^a=\prod_jX_j^{a_j}$ in the product, computed in $\mathbb{N}[X_j : j\in\iota]$.
--
--   The right-hand side counts the ways of choosing $u_k$ or $v_k$ for each $k$ so that every block $j$ is chosen exactly $a_j$ times; it is the multihomogeneous Bézout number of $M$ forms of multidegrees $\mathbf e_{u_k}+\mathbf e_{v_k}$ on $\prod_j\mathbb{P}^{a_j}$. The theorem establishes this bound, in all multidegrees with entries larger than $M$, for the degenerate system in which every form splits into two linear forms with distinct moment-curve parameters. A deformation argument later compares a general system of the same multidegrees with this split one.
--
--   **Formalization Note** The variables are `BlockVariables a = Σ j, Fin (a j + 1)` with the grading `blockWeight` of the first component; $\lambda_j(s)$ is `blockLinearForm a j s`. The pairs form a list `qs` of `FactorPair` structures indexed by `Fin qs.length` (so $k$ runs over $0,\dots,M-1$), $J$ is `productIdeal`, $h_J(d)$ is `pieceDim`, and the product is `mixedPolynomial u v : MvPolynomial ι ℕ` with `a : ι →₀ ℕ`. Since $\ell_k$ is a nonzero form of multidegree $\mathbf e_{u_k}$, its recorded multidegree is necessarily $\mathbf e_{u_k}$, so the hypothesis on the $\delta_k$ always holds in this situation.
-- source:
--   https://github.com/openai/math/blob/1581d4cbdd69a0faf34b2089614fe2a814316a6a/lean/OAI/Algebra/Determinantal/LinearForms.lean#L285-L324

import Mathlib
import Definitions.Def_SmoothInitialForm
import Definitions.Def_OAI_Algebra_Determinantal_Multigraded
import Definitions.Def_OAI_Algebra_Determinantal_LinearForms

open OAI OAI.PermanentBorder OAI.PermanentBorder.Multigraded
open MvPolynomial
variable {K ι σ : Type*} [Field K] [DecidableEq ι]
variable [Fintype ι]

theorem OAI.PermanentBorder.Multigraded.comparison_piece_bound (a : ι →₀ ℕ)
    (qs : List (FactorPair (K := K) (blockWeight (fun v : BlockVariables a => v.1))))
    (u v : Fin qs.length → ι) (t : (Fin qs.length × Bool) → K)
    (ht : Function.Injective t)
    (hleft : ∀ i, (qs.get i).left = blockLinearForm a (u i) (t (i,false)))
    (hright : ∀ i, (qs.get i).right = blockLinearForm a (v i) (t (i,true)))
    (hdeg : ∀ q ∈ qs, ∀ j, q.leftDegree j ≤ 1)
    (hlen : qs.length = ∑ j, a j) (d : ι → ℤ) (hd : ∀ j, (qs.length : ℤ) < d j) :
    pieceDim (blockWeight (fun v : BlockVariables a => v.1))
      (productIdeal (blockWeight (fun v : BlockVariables a => v.1)) qs) d ≤
      (mixedPolynomial u v).coeff a := by sorry
